      "day": "2026-09-20",
      "month": "2026-09",
      "hasDiff": true,
      "ai": {
        "model": "deepseek-v4.1",
        "v": 11,
        "title": "SDK exports rewind run state to the point of an edited user message",
        "summary": "The SDK adds a function that cuts a stored run's `messageHistory` back to the user turn a host is editing, aligning the persisted `RunState` with the transcript a host shows when a user edits an earlier message. It keeps history up to, and not including, the (N+1)-th user message for `keepUserTurns: N` and clones the session state via `cloneSessionState` from `sdk/src/run`, returning null when the history has fewer user messages than the edit position so a caller falls back to clearing state. `contextTokenCount` is rebuilt with `countTokensMessages` because the count is advisory and would otherwise mislead the next turn. Hosted by `@codebuff/sdk` as a public export from `sdk/src/index.ts`.",
        "significance": "notable",
        "audience": "end-users",
        "evidence": "sdk/src/compact-run-state.ts adds a function that counts user messages in `agentState.messageHistory` and slices history up to the (N+1)-th user turn for `keepUserTurns: N`; sdk/src/index.ts re-exports it alongside `compactRunState`.",
        "userVisible": true,
        "migration": "If you maintain a host that edits earlier messages, call this export to truncate `RunState` before resuming the session so the model forgets what the edit removed.",
        "confidence": "high",
        "verify": "passed",
        "selfCheck": "passed",
        "at": "2026-09-27T21:02:35.394Z"
      },
