        "title": "TikTok activation events map to a surface product page instead",
        "summary": "The TikTok branch of buildPaidSocialRequest now reports native coding activation as a CUSTOM web event on the surface's public product page via the new tikTokEventPage helper, so cost-per-activation campaigns can attribute Desktop and CLI runs; activation previously threw 'Native coding activation is not a TikTok website event'. The SendPaidSocialConversionParams type gains a surface field of web, desktop or cli, and tikTokEventPage returns freebuff.com/${surface} for activation while keeping CompleteRegistration on the signed signup path, throwing only when the surface is web or the signup path is unknown. This is the shared paid-social Conversions API path added in 776646ec, which TikTok advertiser reporting flows through.",
